{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And she shall remove her captive's garment.</b> Perhaps because of the beauty of her garment he desired her." "<b>And she shall weep.</b> In order to diminish his desire for her." "<b>A month of days.</b> Perhaps his desire will lighten. And some say <b>and she shall shave</b>, because she is impure, and so too is the law of the metzora." "<b>And she shall do.</b> Tiqqun (trimming). Her trimming is to cut the excess, and likewise 'he did not tend his mustache.' And tiqqun is the essence of every act in Scripture, unless something disgraceful follows it. Also it will be a complete thing." "<b>And she shall remove.</b> For it is defiled." "<b>And she shall dwell in your house and weep.</b> The meaning is: she shall dwell in your house a month of days, weeping." "<b>Her father and her mother.</b> If close. Some say that this weeping is for her father and her mother because they did not convert. And in my opinion, every person is obligated by reason to honor his father and his mother in life and in death." "And the meaning of <b>and she shall weep</b> is that she shall mourn for them according to the law of an Israelite woman, for she converts if they were killed when she was captured. And there is no need to mention 'she shall bathe,' for she requires waters of niddah, for it has already been written 'among you and your captives.'" "And the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: up to three months. And even though there is no need for support, behold the witness: 'and it was like three months' — and that is the time when the offspring begins to move. And it is forbidden to lie with a woman when it is doubtful whether she is pregnant, because of the offspring, for there are some who give birth lacking two months, and also in excess — but this is rare." "<b>A month of days.</b> Like חדש ימים. I have already explained it. And the month is called ירח because its principal is the moon."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {3 "The phrase 'לא עשה שפמו' is a partial biblical citation, apparently referencing a verse about not trimming the mustache; the specific verse reference is not given by Ibn Ezra here.", 6 "'אם קרוב' is obscure in context; translated hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt or elliptical.", 7 "'כי היא מתייהדת אם נהרגו' is translated literally; the syntactic connection between conversion and the parents' death is left as Ibn Ezra gives it.", 8 "'ואע״פ שאין צורך לחזק הנה העד' is rendered hyper-literally; the logical connection between the rabbinic ruling and the biblical proof from 'and it was like three months' is left compressed as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:21.069163906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}